From af27ded935c7ac58f9e4b3e5b294fc8bf3b05e2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 17:19:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 52/56] drm/gma500: blame an sgxfive BIF fault on the faulting
 directory's job

A recovery blamed the owner of the oldest unfinished job. With render jobs
that is not always the job that faulted: the firmware runs a transfer
queued after a render ahead of the render's 3D work, so a transfer that
faults while an older render waits for the 3D pipe made the render's
context lost, and the transfer faulted again when it was re-run.

BIF_FAULT names the directory list the fault went through (bits 3:0), and
that list's DIR_LIST_BASE register holds the page directory the firmware
put there, i.e. the faulting VM's. The fault watchdog now reads that
directory when it first sees a fault and blames the oldest unfinished job
on it; when the fault names no client directory (the EDM's own list 15,
a directory no context uses, or one with nothing unfinished) it falls back
to the oldest job of all, as before. Contexts keep their VM's directory
address for this. A recovery now checks that the suspect is still its
context's oldest unfinished job, not the oldest of all, so the detector
that loses a race still blames no one.

On the laptop a transfer faulting from another file while a render waits
loses only its own context; the render completes exactly.

Assisted-by: LLM
